  "authoringNote": "D1 identity regression (checkpoint #27, moved to a supporting note by recorded ruling 4 so that only R02 changes). The note passes R09 (hash, MIME and exact body valid; the padded name is valid ExactText), so R02 compares its stated values exactly: the identifier equals the case subject but \"Peyton Testcase \" differs from \"Peyton Testcase\" by its trailing space, with no trimming. R02 is conflict with one condition, binding.stated_name naming f08x3-note v1; the parent set and quarantine list are that version only. The quarantined note is never cited, so R02 cites the six facts of the encounter, order and receipt. No other rule reads notes, so R01, R03, R04, R05 and R07 pass with ordinary citations (eight, nine, six, four, one), R09 passes, R06 and R10 as always. State needs_human_review.",
